# The backend Dockerfile does `COPY . .` (no ignore file today), baking tests,
# caches, and agent notes into the image. Exclude everything the runtime doesn't
# need — smaller images, faster pulls, less attack surface (gameplan 2.1).
#
# CI mounts the test files back in from the checkout (gameplan 8.1), so dropping
# them here doesn't stop the image from being tested.

# Test suite + its tooling (pytest lives in test-requirements.txt, not the image)
tests/
pytest.ini
test-requirements.txt
.pytest_cache/

# Agent working notes — never a runtime dependency
agents/

# Python bytecode / caches (**/ so nested dirs like app/__pycache__ match too —
# dockerignore patterns are rooted at the context, unlike .gitignore)
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo

# Env files (secrets are materialized from SSM at deploy, gameplan 5.2; the
# .example templates are dev docs, not needed in the image)
.env*

# Local certs / scratch material — private keys don't belong in any image layer
**/*.pem

# Keep (do NOT ignore): app/ incl. app/models/*.pb (runtime TF model), alembic/,
# alembic.ini, backend_requirements.txt — all load-bearing at runtime.
